\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Schematic plan view of the four detector layouts on the \SI {250}{\milli \meter }$\times $\SI {250}{\milli \meter } plate footprint. Black squares mark the side-mounted SiPMs (drawn oversized for visibility; the active area is \SI {4}{\milli \meter }$\times $\SI {4}{\milli \meter }), and the dashed grey lines are the $x=0$, $y=0$ axes. Config~1 places two SiPMs on each of the four edges; config~2 places one SiPM per edge at the same offsets as config~1 (one device removed per side); config~3 places both SiPMs on the top ($+y$, report frame) edge; config~4 uses a single SiPM reading out a WLS fibre clamp on the same top edge, with the read-out SiPM at its left end (green bar), following Fig.~3(b) of Ref.~\cite  {Rao2025}. In the simulation frame both configs~3 and~4 sit on the $-x$ narrow face (the report plan view maps $(x,y)\to (y,-x)$). The inwards-offset labels name the eight side-mounted sensors (T/B/R/L $=$ top/bottom/right/left); on each edge ``1'' marks the sensor nearer the corner reached when travelling clockwise around the perimeter, so ``1'' sits at the top-right (T1), bottom-right (R1), bottom-left (B1) and top-left (L1) corners. This is the scheme used in the light-sharing discussion below. The same black-square markers are overlaid on the collection-efficiency maps of Figs.~\ref {fig:wholeslab}--\ref {fig:wholeslab4}.}}{7}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:layouts}{{1}{7}{Schematic plan view of the four detector layouts on the \SI {250}{\milli \meter }$\times $\SI {250}{\milli \meter } plate footprint. Black squares mark the side-mounted SiPMs (drawn oversized for visibility; the active area is \SI {4}{\milli \meter }$\times $\SI {4}{\milli \meter }), and the dashed grey lines are the $x=0$, $y=0$ axes. Config~1 places two SiPMs on each of the four edges; config~2 places one SiPM per edge at the same offsets as config~1 (one device removed per side); config~3 places both SiPMs on the top ($+y$, report frame) edge; config~4 uses a single SiPM reading out a WLS fibre clamp on the same top edge, with the read-out SiPM at its left end (green bar), following Fig.~3(b) of Ref.~\cite {Rao2025}. In the simulation frame both configs~3 and~4 sit on the $-x$ narrow face (the report plan view maps $(x,y)\to (y,-x)$). The inwards-offset labels name the eight side-mounted sensors (T/B/R/L $=$ top/bottom/right/left); on each edge ``1'' marks the sensor nearer the corner reached when travelling clockwise around the perimeter, so ``1'' sits at the top-right (T1), bottom-right (R1), bottom-left (B1) and top-left (L1) corners. This is the scheme used in the light-sharing discussion below. The same black-square markers are overlaid on the collection-efficiency maps of Figs.~\ref {fig:wholeslab}--\ref {fig:wholeslab4}}{figure.caption.2}{}}
