\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces The response as a function of the distance to the nearest collection site. Each panel is one layout; the abscissa is the distance $d$ from the muon's entry point to the nearest SiPM tile (configs~1--3) or to the WLS fibre line along the top edge (config~4), and the ordinate is the collection efficiency normalised to the plate average of the same layout and treatment. The dashed line is the plate average. The four treatments share one shape and differ only in level: the specular wrappers are flat because they mix the light thoroughly, while the diffuse paint and the contact-limited bare plate are brightest close to a sensor and fall away from it. Error bars are the propagated Poisson uncertainties.}}{40}{figure.caption.33}\protected@file@percent }
